  "description": "Three of template 35's imagers in Sun-synchronous planes 30 deg apart, reaching the pole together, sharing a Svalbard and a Berlin station that serve one spacecraft at a time, for two days. Any of them may take a target.\n\nWhat to look at:\n- Run > Plan: 33 passes are wanted by two or three spacecraft; each spacecraft gets 11 contacts.\n- The station rows of the chart: whose contact each pass holds.\n- Requests not placed: passes lost to a busy station, and the European targets that conflict with contacts.\n\nTry changing:\n- One spacecraft's contact priority to 1 and the others' to 2: it takes the contested passes.\n- The stations' capacity to 2: two spacecraft at a time.",
